note ogmask for the CPU-only targets (aarch64, x86linux, x86efi). model.om calls it only when
note ogkm[0] = 1, which only gpu/gg.om's gcmp2 sets, so reaching it is a defect: exit 2.
fn ogmask yo ulong l ulong t ulong to void
exit 2
end

note ogchip and oglast (cli.om ochipup, olastf) run only when ogpu[0] = 1, which only gpu/gg.om's
note gserve and gsample set, so reaching them on a CPU-only target is a defect: exit 2.
fn ogchip to void
exit 2
end

fn oglast to void
exit 2
end
